	skos:definition	"a meeting of the inhabitants of a town"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08312462-n .

<i80820>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"(Christianity) an assembly of theologians and bishops and other representatives of different churches or dioceses that is convened to regulate matters of discipline or doctrine"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08312559-n .

<i80821>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"(early Christian church) one of seven gatherings of bishops from around the known world under the presidency of the Pope to regulate matters of faith and morals and discipline"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08312988-n .

<i80822>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the first ecumenical council in 325 which produced the wording of the Nicene Creed and condemned the heresy of Arianism"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08313592-n .

<i80823>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the second ecumenical council in 381 which added wording about the Holy Spirit to the Nicene Creed"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08313790-n .

<i80824>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the third ecumenical council in 431 which declared Mary as mother of God and condemned Pelagius"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08313983-n .

<i80825>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the fourth ecumenical council in 451 which defined the two natures (human and divine) of Christ"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08314153-n .

<i80826>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the fifth ecumenical council in 553 which held Origen's writings to be heretic"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08314327-n .

<i80827>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the sixth ecumenical council in 680-681 which condemned Monothelitism by defining two wills in Christ, divine and human"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08314501-n .

<i80828>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the seventh ecumenical council in 787 which refuted iconoclasm and regulated the veneration of holy images"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08314715-n .

<i80829>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council in 869 that condemned Photius who had become the patriarch of Constantinople without approval from the Vatican, thereby precipitating the schism between the eastern and western churches"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08314901-n .

<i80830>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"any of five general councils of the Western Catholic Church that were held in the Lateran Palace"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08315194-n .

<i80831>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the first council of the Western Church held in the Lateran Palace in 1123; focused on church discipline and made plans to recover the Holy Lands from the Muslim `infidels'"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08315442-n .

<i80832>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the second council of the Western Church in 1139 which put an end to the dogmatic errors of Arnold of Brescia"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08315682-n .

<i80833>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the Lateran Council in 1179 that condemned the heresies of the Albigenses and the Waldenses"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08315860-n .

<i80834>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the Lateran Council in 1215 was the most important council of the Middle Ages; issued a creed against Albigensianism, published reformatory decrees, promulgated the doctrine of transubstantiation, and clarified church doctrine on the Trinity and Incarnation"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08316019-n .

<i80835>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council of the Western Church in 1245 that excommunicated Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II and planned a new crusade against the Holy Land"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08316346-n .

<i80836>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council in 1274 that effected a temporary reunion of the Greek Orthodox with the Roman Catholic Church"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08316564-n .

<i80837>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council in 1311-1313 that dealt with alleged crimes of the Knights Templar, planned a new crusade, and took on the reformation of the clergy"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08316748-n .

<i80838>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council in 1414-1418 that succeeded in ending the Great Schism in the Roman Catholic Church"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08316965-n .

<i80839>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council in 1431-1439 that concentrated on the elimination of heresies and on reforms within the Roman Catholic Church"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08317139-n .

<i80840>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the council in 1512-1517 that published disciplinary decrees and planned (but did not carry out) a crusade against Turkey"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08317340-n .

<i80841>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"a council of the Roman Catholic Church convened in Trento in three sessions between 1545 and 1563 to examine and condemn the teachings of Martin Luther and other Protestant reformers; redefined the Roman Catholic doctrine and abolished various ecclesiastical abuses and strengthened the papacy"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08317529-n .

<i80842>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"each of two councils of the Roman Catholic Church"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08317885-n .

<i80843>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the Vatican Council in 1869-1870 that proclaimed the infallibility of the pope when speaking ex cathedra"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08318032-n .

<i80844>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"the Vatican Council in 1962-1965 that abandoned the universal Latin liturgy and acknowledged ecumenism and made other reforms"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:08318216-n .

