	skos:definition	"god of the winds in ancient mythology"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09553490-n .

<i86862>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"personification of the sky or upper air breathed by the Olympians; son of Erebus and night or of Chaos and darkness"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09553599-n .

<i86863>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) Greek god of light; god of prophecy and poetry and music and healing; son of Zeus and Leto; twin brother of Artemis"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09553767-n .

<i86864>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"epithet for Apollo; from the dragon Python which he killed"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09554019-n .

<i86865>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"goddess of love and beauty and daughter of Zeus in ancient mythology; identified with Roman Venus"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09554132-n .

<i86866>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) priestess of Aphrodite who killed herself when her lover Leander drowned while trying to swim the Hellespont to see her"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09554297-n .

<i86867>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) a youth beloved of Hero who drowned in a storm in the Hellespont on one of his nightly visits to see her"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09554505-n .

<i86868>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) a king who created a statue of a woman and fell in love with it; Aphrodite brought the sculpture to life as Galatea"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09554701-n .

<i86869>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) a maiden who was first a sculpture created by Pygmalion and was brought to life by Aphrodite in answer to Pygmalion's prayers"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09554910-n .

<i86870>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"goddess of love; counterpart of Greek Aphrodite"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555127-n .

<i86871>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) Greek god of war; son of Zeus and Hera; identified with Roman Mars"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555236-n .

<i86872>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) goddess of discord; sister of Ares"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555391-n .

<i86873>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) the Greek personification of death; son of Nyx"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555514-n .

<i86874>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Roman mythology) Roman god of death; counterpart of Thanatos"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555653-n .

<i86875>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Roman mythology) Roman god of war and agriculture; father of Romulus and Remus; counterpart of Greek Ares"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555785-n .

<i86876>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) Greek goddess of the night; daughter of Chaos; counterpart of Roman Nox"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09555962-n .

<i86877>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"(Roman mythology) a vestal virgin who became the mother by Mars of the twins Romulus and Remus"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09556121-n .

<i86878>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Roman mythology) founder of Rome; suckled with his twin brother Remus by a wolf after their parents (Mars and Rhea Silvia) abandoned them; Romulus killed Remus in an argument over the building of Rome"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09556305-n .

<i86879>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Roman mythology) the twin brother of Romulus"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09556580-n .

<i86880>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) the virgin goddess of the hunt and the Moon; daughter of Leto and twin sister of Apollo; identified with Roman Diana"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09556697-n .

<i86881>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) the god who personified the north wind"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09556915-n .

<i86882>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Roman mythology) virgin goddess of the hunt and the Moon; counterpart of Greek Artemis"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09557130-n .

<i86883>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"goddess of criminal rashness and its punishment"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09557289-n .

<i86884>	a	<Instance> ;
	skos:definition	"(Greek mythology) goddess of wisdom and useful arts and prudent warfare; guardian of Athens; identified with Roman Minerva"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:09557387-n .

<i86885>	a	<Instance> ;
