<i97585>	a	<Concept> ;
	skos:definition	"any effect that seems to be a consequence of administering a placebo; the change is usually beneficial and is assumed result from the person's faith in the treatment or preconceptions about what the experimental drug was supposed to do; pharmacologists were the first to talk about placebo effects but now the idea has been generalized to many situations having nothing to do with drugs"@en ;
	dc:source	pwn30:11416087-n .

